{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Aaron lifted his hands</b> — he merited the gifts of priesthood." "<b>And he blessed them</b> — three blessings corresponding to three types of offerings. The first blessing corresponding to the sin-offering: \"May He guard you\" — from sin, as it is said: רגלי חסידיו ישמור (He guards the feet of His faithful). \"May He shine\" — corresponding to the burnt-offering, as it is said: בעלותך לראות (when you go up to see). \"Peace\" — corresponding to the peace-offerings."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:04.720122344Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}